  => the core's resonance energy is carried by the length-3 (3-term v_a+v_b=v_c) fusions —
     the dynamical-face resonances. This is what no measure bound can push below `main`.

[3] THE SIDESTEP: the high-energy core is lonely by CONSTRUCTION at the rational sieve t=a/n
  config              | E≥main (energy fails) | sieve witness t=a/n | gap there | = 1/n (tight)?
  AP {1..5} core      | True                  | t=1/6             | 0.1667    | YES (the n-gon vertex, measure-0 witness)
  AP {1..6} core      | True                  | t=1/7             | 0.1429    | YES (the n-gon vertex, measure-0 witness)
  Fibonacci 1,2,3,5,8 | True                  | t=1/6             | 0.1667    | YES (the n-gon vertex, measure-0 witness)
  generic 3,5,11,17,29 | False                 | t=3/6             | 0.5000    | gap>1/n (bulk, also fine)
  Sidon 1,2,5,11,22   | False                 | t=2/6             | 0.3333    | gap>1/n (bulk, also fine)
  transl {7..11}      | False                 | t=1/6             | 0.1667    | YES (the n-gon vertex, measure-0 witness)
  => where the resonance energy is too large to bound (the core), the rational sieve t=a/n
     EXHIBITS the witness directly — sidestepping the energy. (Vitali boundary HYP-2054.)

[4] THE TWO FACES (S602) of the sidestep
  DYNAMICAL face = the resonance energy E(v) = Σ over the relation lattice (resonances);
                   a MEASURE quantity; proves the BULK; BLIND to the measure-0 core (Vitali).
  ADDITIVE  face = the construction: sieve t=a/n, the mod-(2n-1) transversal rigidity (64
                   classes all lonely). Handles the CORE; SIDESTEPS the resonance energy.
  => LRC = bulk (bound the resonance energy) ⊔ core (sidestep it by construction). One
     concept (resonance energy), one boundary (Vitali), two faces (measure ⊔ construction).
